Package: eccmr
Type: Package
Title: Error-Correcting Code Inspired Robust Mendelian Randomization
Version: 0.3.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Junhong", "Jiang", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "linzenan@njmu.edu.cn"),
    person("Di", "Hu", role = "aut"),
    person("Qi", "Zhang", role = "aut"),
    person("Zenan", "Lin", role = "aut"),
    person("Mu-BioDig Group", role = "cph"))
Description: Implements ECC-MR, an error-correcting code inspired framework
    for robust Mendelian randomization with GWAS summary statistics. Horizontal
    pleiotropy is treated as sparse, correctable corruption of SNP-level causal
    signals, and linkage disequilibrium (LD) among instruments is exploited as
    structured redundancy: a parity-check matrix is built from the LD graph so
    that the causal signal lies in its null space, while pleiotropy generates a
    nonzero syndrome. The causal effect and the sparse pleiotropic effects are
    estimated jointly by convex optimization (inverse-variance weighted least
    squares + L1 sparsity + syndrome-consistency penalty), with tuning by a
    BIC criterion along the penalty path (LD-block cross-validation
    optional), a relaxed debiasing refit, and inference by LD-block
    bootstrap. A syndrome-based global test of pleiotropy is also provided,
    together with reference implementations of mainstream MR methods (IVW,
    MR-Egger, weighted median, MR-Lasso) and simulation utilities for
    benchmarking ECC-MR against them, including an operating-boundary
    scan across pleiotropy regimes (run_boundary_scan).
